From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] su: build with USE_BSM_AUDIT on Apple platforms

su.c records its events with audit_submit(3) under USE_BSM_AUDIT, as
FreeBSD's su does, but Apple builds it without (it reports to
EndpointSecurity instead), and the Apple block declares auid for its own
getauid() call, a second declaration once USE_BSM_AUDIT is defined too.
NeoDarwin has no EndpointSecurity and builds su with USE_BSM_AUDIT
(docs/base/session.md, "BSM audit"): declare auid once.

--- a/su/su.c
+++ b/su/su.c
@@ -219,7 +219,9 @@
 	au_id_t		 auid;
 #endif
 #ifdef __APPLE__
+#ifndef USE_BSM_AUDIT
 	au_id_t		 auid;
+#endif /* !USE_BSM_AUDIT */
 	/* 4043304 */
 	const char	*avshell;
 	char		avshellbuf[MAXPATHLEN];
